{"id": "abec7d03-236b-4f17-9934-6beb8c4dd9ac", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T11:20:49.849321", "source": "user", "parent_id": "a956ceaa-d5de-4876-8260-9fd13ea4c6c6", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"巡检结果和方案纲要已阅，整体思路正确，可以推进到最终实验设计。为使下一步交付物可以直接落地，请先把以下不确定性锁定为可操作的设计默认值，并在最终方案中以这些默认值为基准来写 sweep grid 与表/图规范。1）方法语义：1F1B-I 采用 v=2 的交错实现；ZB-1p 与 ZB-2p 采用 Qi et al. 2023 中定义的 1-pass / 2-pass 权值梯度切分。若定义与此不同，请在方案中显式标注。2）M 扫描的批量口径：固定全局批量 GBS，反向缩放 microbatch size（mbs = GBS / M），不再另行使用梯度累积。3）M 取值：在 [8, 16, 32, 64, 128] 的对数刻度上扫描（若调度合法性约束 M ≥ P，则以 M ∈ {8, 16, 32, 64, 128}∩[P,∞) 为准，并写明约束）。4）M 计数对象：一个优化步中流水线处理的微批数，不包含任何外层累积。5）Warm-up 处理：稳态起算后固定 N 个 micro-steps 排除后开始计时；启动序列独立记录；ZB-2p 的长 tail 必须单独报告 warm-up 耗时与微步数。6）吞吐量口径：同时报告 samples/sec 和 tokens/sec，覆盖通信时间；以单卡平均与全局两套口径并列呈现。7）预设：在最终方案中固定一组代表性硬件/拓扑（如单节点 8 卡 NVLink、pipeline degree P=4、GPT-类模型的一组中等规模/精度/dtype），把其他 P 与模型规模列为敏感性补充实验，避免在主设计中铺得太开。8）变体超参数：1F1B-I 与 ZB-2p 的 v 默认取 2，并在方法描述段显式标注。9）重复与统计：每 (method, M) 单元重复 ≥3 次；若因调度确定性强导致 seed 方差为 0，也应在方案中记为方法层面假设，并在最终报告里说明其影响；检验使用方法内 Spearman 单调性检验 + 方法×M 交互检验，配合方法内最小二乘斜率符号。10）协报告指标：在主表中同时给出吞吐、气泡占比（理论或实测）、峰值显存、单步耗时、warm-up 长度。请基于以上默认值，产出最终实验设计：含一句话研究问题、变量与口径定义、固定参数清单、M 扫描网格（含越界回退规则）、重复/统计方案、表与图布局（建议至少包含一张 throughput-vs-M 折线图加一张以 M 为分组的柱状图，以及一张原始数据 + 汇总统计的主表）、可行性说明（说明这是设计任务，不必实际执行），并把当前轮回中仍未解决的剩余疑问以最多 3 条的形式附在文末。\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"result\", \"approach_approved\": true}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 20}
{"id": "9b0a0f27-0c13-4409-a7d8-9e896561c4bf", "timestamp": "2026-10-23T11:23:02.619506", "source": "agent", "parent_id": "abec7d03-236b-4f17-9934-6beb8c4dd9ac", "action": {"stage": "result", "answer": "Final experiment design produced and aligned to the researcher's 10 locked defaults. Specification summary:\n\n- **Research question (one sentence).** Holding model, hardware, DP, and global batch size fixed, does steady-state training throughput (samples/sec, global and per-card) rise monotonically with `M ∈ {8, 16, 32, 64, 128}` for `1F1B`, `1F1B-I(v=2)`, and `ZB-1p`, while `ZB-2p (wpasses=2)` already sits at a high throughput at small `M` and exhibits a near-flat throughput-vs-M curve?\n\n- **Variables & metrics.** IV: `method ∈ {1F1B, 1F1B-I(v=2), ZB-1p, ZB-2p(wpasses=2)}` × `M ∈ {8,16,32,64,128}` (20 cells). DV: throughput in samples/sec AND tokens/sec, both global and per-card, computed over `K=30` opt-steps after `N=5`-microstep warm-up exclusion, communication time **included**. Co-reported: theoretical + measured bubble fraction, peak memory per rank, time/step, warm-up microsteps and time (separately for ZB-2p).\n\n- **Fixed parameters.** Hardware: 1 node, 8× ≥40 GB GPUs, NVLink/NVSwitch. P=4, DP=2 (DP×P=8). v=2 (1F1B-I), wpasses=2 (ZB-2p). GPT-style medium: L=24, H=1024, A=16, FFN=4096, V=50257, S=2048, ~340M params. bf16 fwd/bwd, fp32 master + accumulators, AdamW, FlashAttention-2 or SDPA, activation checkpointing **off** in main, ZeRO/FSDP **off**. GBS=128 sequences ⇒ mbs=128/M is integer for every M.\n\n- **M scan grid.** 5 log-scale M values, all satisfy `M ≥ P=4` so no level is dropped in main design; mbs is integer for every level. Out-of-grid fallback rules documented (legal-schedule `M ≥ P`, `mbs ≥ 1` floor, per-stage memory ceiling split-row, `wpasses` constraint `M ≥ P × wpasses` for ZB-2p).\n\n- **Repeat & statistics.** R=3 seeds per cell, Latin-square ordering. 60 main runs. Tests: per-method Spearman one-sided `ρ>0` (Bonferroni across 3 rising